lms tend to focus on the grunts the  enlisted infantrymen who are just cogs  and a much larger machine  they are the everyman tom hanks is a  schoolteacher in saving private ryan and  the main characters in the deer hunter  are steel mill workers  these films tell the stories of average  joes who get caught up in the chaos and  can't wait to go home  you know if going to ramel and finding  him so he can go home if that earns me  the right to get back to my wife well  then  then that's my mission in direct  contrast iraq war films are about people  who want to be there and sometimes they  actually thrive in the chaos  without a draft the iraq war was more  removed from everyday american life  adding the fact that a large part of the  military in the middle east was made up  of mercenary contractors and the  american army turned into a job for just  a select few who chose to be there iraq  war movies center on a warrior class of  specialized units such as in the film's  american sniper zero dark 30 and the  hurt locker  got tools got two all right let's rock  and roll man  sergeant james in the hurlocker  perfectly embodies the warrior-class  mentality of american soldiers in the  iraq war  he's a specialized elite soldier  equipped to deal with the exact nature  of the war  in his first scene in combat he expertly  diffuses a massive roadside bomb  right off the bat we see he has the  technical expertise that an enlisted  soldier would not have  and his technical expertise applies to  more than just diffusing the bomb itself  before he defuses the bomb he also  defuses a tense situation with an iraqi  civilian  the film sets up sergeant james as a  warrior soldier that can do it all  he not only defuses bombs he also  defuses conflict  so a key genre element of many iraq war  films is the painting of american  soldiers as vocational well-trained  warriors that can deal with both combat  and civilian occupation  american sniper focuses on a highly  specialized sniper 