ight  the violence that happens abroad is  abstract and removed from the american  people  films like the hurlocker and american  sniper represent an escapist desire to  create clear lines between good and evil  in the middle east but the reality is  far more complex there's still plenty of  time for more films like jarhead  to come out that bring a more nuanced  take on ideas of heroism and violence  and i think they will but while that  happens we're all still in the desert  if you liked the topic of this video we  also recorded a podcast episode  talking more in depth about war movies  click on the link in the description to  listen to it yourself  and give us feedback on what you think  and as always a big thanks to our  patreon supporters who watched this  video a week in advance and got early  access to the podcast  thanks for watching

